WEBVTT

00:07.173 --> 00:08.925
Father, what is this?

00:09.009 --> 00:12.053
A passageway connecting
the Left and Right to the keep.

00:12.137 --> 00:13.179
I had no clue this was here.

00:13.930 --> 00:19.894
The lord had this secret passageway made
back when this village was a castle.

00:19.978 --> 00:22.689
Only a few people know about it.

00:23.356 --> 00:25.525
Don't tell anyone else.

00:25.608 --> 00:27.694
Only use it when you have to.

00:30.447 --> 00:34.451
The Left and Right's bases at
the village exit are above us.

00:37.454 --> 00:38.705
Listen to me, Yuru.

00:38.788 --> 00:43.918
The Left and Right
are always watching over you.

00:45.044 --> 00:48.006
We've been here watchin' you
this whole time, Yuru.

00:48.089 --> 00:51.968
Henceforth, we are your Daemons.

00:52.761 --> 00:55.764
You're... the Left and Right?

02:29.107 --> 02:32.235
So this crybaby is our master?

02:32.318 --> 02:35.989
Don't, Right. You're upsetting our master.

02:36.072 --> 02:37.448
Hello, Left and Right.

02:38.074 --> 02:39.033
Nice to meet you.

02:39.117 --> 02:41.161
You're Dera, the Daemon retainer.

02:41.244 --> 02:43.454
We've been watching you, too.

02:43.955 --> 02:48.334
We took down those birds
since they seemed to be harmin' you,

02:48.418 --> 02:50.169
but what were they?

02:50.253 --> 02:52.714
They're vehicles of the
modern world below.

02:52.797 --> 02:54.966
But we don't have time to chat.

02:55.592 --> 02:58.511
At least two threats have shown up.

02:58.595 --> 03:01.556
Help us get down the mountain
quickly and safely.

03:01.639 --> 03:02.473
Dera.

03:03.182 --> 03:05.393
You are not our master.

03:05.476 --> 03:07.729
Our master is Yuru.

03:07.812 --> 03:09.355
We obey his orders.

03:09.439 --> 03:13.151
I know, but there's no time to
explain the situation to him.

03:13.234 --> 03:14.611
Ugh.

03:15.820 --> 03:17.614
Those look strong.

03:17.697 --> 03:20.283
Whose Daemons are you? The old guy's?

03:20.366 --> 03:21.993
What is that tooth monster?!

03:22.076 --> 03:23.912
What did I tell you? They're here!

03:23.995 --> 03:26.623
And they're perfectly fine after
I hit them with a grenade!

03:27.206 --> 03:28.875
Don't underestimate my Daemons' toughness.

03:29.542 --> 03:31.127
And don't call them monsters. Rude.

03:32.211 --> 03:33.338
Let's see...

03:33.838 --> 03:36.549
A sixteen-year-old boy. Are you Yuru?

03:36.633 --> 03:38.843
Me? I'm seventeen.

03:38.927 --> 03:40.428
By traditional counting.

03:40.511 --> 03:41.804
The world below considers you sixteen.

03:41.888 --> 03:42.889
What's that?

03:42.972 --> 03:45.600
I see. So you're Asa's brother.

03:47.018 --> 03:47.852
Asa?

03:52.273 --> 03:54.442
I'm here to kill everyone else.

03:55.777 --> 03:57.695
Why don't you come with me?

03:59.781 --> 04:02.450
Are you the ones who
killed the villagers?

04:02.533 --> 04:03.993
We sure are.

04:04.744 --> 04:09.832
Master Yuru, give the word,
and we'll do whatever you command.

04:09.916 --> 04:12.293
I won't command you to do anything.

04:13.211 --> 04:15.088
You're the village's guardian deities.

04:15.171 --> 04:17.423
I wouldn't dare give you orders.

04:20.051 --> 04:23.263
But I do have two requests.

04:23.805 --> 04:27.725
First, there should be survivors.

04:27.809 --> 04:30.311
Take them to a safe place.

04:30.895 --> 04:33.606
And second...

04:34.565 --> 04:37.860
That runt is mine. Don't touch her.

04:39.279 --> 04:42.448
Aside from that, do as you please.

04:44.742 --> 04:46.202
Lucky us, Left.

04:46.786 --> 04:49.706
Our new master is hands off.

04:50.456 --> 04:52.208
Understood!

05:02.468 --> 05:03.886
Granny Yamaha.

05:04.679 --> 05:07.640
We'll never forgive you.

05:08.266 --> 05:10.685
You'll pay for what you've done.

05:25.742 --> 05:27.493
He's hands off.

05:28.077 --> 05:29.704
Understood!

05:34.417 --> 05:36.586
I'll take the villagers to a safe place.

05:37.295 --> 05:40.089
Watch out. My other half is hot-blooded.

05:44.677 --> 05:45.845
What?!

05:48.056 --> 05:50.058
I'm just following my master's orders.

05:50.725 --> 05:52.602
I'll do as I please.

05:58.941 --> 06:00.359
A second arrow!

06:07.992 --> 06:10.036
Those Daemons are tough.

06:10.119 --> 06:11.746
- I'll go get her!
- Hey!

06:11.829 --> 06:12.872
Oh, come on!

06:12.955 --> 06:14.290
Why is this happening?

06:14.373 --> 06:16.042
I'm begging you, let's
get off this mountain.

06:26.427 --> 06:29.514
Hey, are you alive? Hey.

06:32.767 --> 06:34.560
Oh, you are alive.

06:38.689 --> 06:40.733
This must be someone else's blood.

06:40.817 --> 06:43.236
You're uninjured. That's good.

06:46.697 --> 06:51.160
Oh, right. You can't see me.

06:53.162 --> 06:56.374
Don't worry. I'm no monster.

06:56.457 --> 06:59.877
I'll take you somewhere safe.

07:01.921 --> 07:02.880
Oh?

07:06.384 --> 07:07.468
Seriously?

07:07.552 --> 07:10.638
Everyone fainted when they saw me.

07:10.721 --> 07:12.473
That hurts, you know?

07:13.724 --> 07:18.688
They showed no mercy to the adults,
but they didn't hurt the kids.

07:23.234 --> 07:25.278
You can see me, can't you?

07:39.917 --> 07:41.627
Not even a hello?

07:42.420 --> 07:44.755
That's a dangerous power you've got there.

07:44.839 --> 07:48.634
I'll give you a fight if that's what
you want, but my master's orders—

07:52.305 --> 07:55.475
Kids these days just don't listen!

08:00.855 --> 08:02.315
That girl...

08:16.287 --> 08:19.415
You can't be serious!
It's two against one!

08:40.895 --> 08:42.271
A second one?!

08:44.065 --> 08:44.941
Asa!

08:54.242 --> 08:55.076
Damn it!

08:56.244 --> 08:57.453
Gabby-chan!

08:58.579 --> 09:00.873
Thanks, Asa.

09:00.957 --> 09:01.916
Don't move!

09:05.419 --> 09:07.338
Who are you? Speak.

09:07.421 --> 09:10.174
I'm your sister, Asa, Brother.

09:10.258 --> 09:13.052
Liar! Asa's not that big!

09:13.135 --> 09:16.639
The world below has better
access to nutrition.

09:16.722 --> 09:18.933
Asa doesn't glare like that.

09:19.016 --> 09:20.059
I've been through a lot.

09:20.142 --> 09:21.852
I'm jaded, okay?

09:23.354 --> 09:24.647
Hey!

09:24.730 --> 09:27.567
Ain't good for family to fight!

09:33.155 --> 09:37.118
This girl's blood smells
just like yours, Yuru.

09:37.201 --> 09:39.704
- You're siblings.
- What?!

09:40.329 --> 09:43.791
Then who's the Asa up in the keep?

09:43.874 --> 09:45.293
An impostor.

09:48.212 --> 09:54.302
Ten years ago, after our parents
took me and fled the village,

09:54.385 --> 09:58.639
Granny and the others feared
you'd run away, too.

10:01.100 --> 10:06.105
So they created an impostor
to keep you here.

10:07.148 --> 10:09.567
You're a kind and caring older brother.

10:09.650 --> 10:13.404
You wouldn't leave as long as
Asa was still in the village.

10:14.822 --> 10:17.908
That Asa is fake.

10:29.587 --> 10:32.923
Now that you've had your touching reunion,

10:33.007 --> 10:36.218
do you mind backing off, Asa-chan?

10:36.302 --> 10:37.637
Dera-san!

10:37.720 --> 10:39.889
You're the one they're after.

10:39.972 --> 10:43.809
We still don't know what the
allegedly real Asa is capable of.

10:43.893 --> 10:47.855
And if you stay, the village
could suffer more damage.

10:49.065 --> 10:51.525
There are still survivors, right?

11:00.242 --> 11:01.202
Hey.

11:02.536 --> 11:04.872
Don't hurt any more villagers.

11:04.955 --> 11:08.000
I'll let the runt go, so withdraw.

11:10.461 --> 11:12.004
- Fine.
- Asa!

11:12.671 --> 11:13.714
Later.

11:23.641 --> 11:25.017
Ow...

11:25.101 --> 11:27.478
Why aren't we capturing him?

11:27.561 --> 11:32.650
Because your wounds need tending,
and we know he's safe now.

11:32.733 --> 11:34.318
Ow...

11:34.402 --> 11:35.236
Are you okay?

11:36.237 --> 11:41.534
You know, your brother sure is merciless.

11:41.617 --> 11:42.451
Yeah.

11:43.452 --> 11:45.955
- He's skilled.
- Yeah.

11:46.622 --> 11:47.873
He's alive.

11:48.374 --> 11:49.208
Yeah.

11:50.835 --> 11:51.961
He's alive.

11:56.549 --> 11:59.343
My brother's alive.

12:19.697 --> 12:21.282
The barrier is returning.

12:22.199 --> 12:23.742
We should get off the mountain quickly.

12:43.095 --> 12:45.014
Those helicopters sure were loud.

12:45.097 --> 12:46.474
What was that about?

12:47.057 --> 12:49.143
Maybe someone needed rescuing.

12:49.643 --> 12:53.063
A lot of people go missing
in these mountains.

12:53.147 --> 12:55.608
A bunch of them have never been found.

12:56.442 --> 12:57.943
Maybe it's like that spooky story.

12:58.027 --> 13:00.696
You know the one...

13:00.779 --> 13:01.697
The lost village!

13:01.780 --> 13:02.615
Yeah, that.

13:03.199 --> 13:07.578
Hikers suddenly wander into another world.

13:07.661 --> 13:10.414
There's a village where
there shouldn't be one.

13:10.498 --> 13:14.376
Even if they go back later,
there's no trace of it.

13:14.960 --> 13:16.587
Hello!

13:16.670 --> 13:17.505
Oh.

13:18.214 --> 13:19.465
Hello.

13:19.548 --> 13:21.175
Were those mountain porters?

13:21.258 --> 13:22.801
Or traditional hunters?

13:22.885 --> 13:23.969
OLD HIGASHI VILLAGE TRAILHEAD

13:24.053 --> 13:25.137
The wind's so strong.

13:25.221 --> 13:26.805
Let's hike back down.

13:30.518 --> 13:31.727
We can't see the village anymore.

13:32.311 --> 13:34.522
It must be back inside the barrier.

13:34.605 --> 13:36.482
Can we not go back?

13:36.982 --> 13:39.693
You could if you really wanted to.

13:40.778 --> 13:44.490
But someone who knew where to find
it broke through the barrier.

13:44.573 --> 13:48.786
They were after you, so there's
no point in hiding there.

13:48.869 --> 13:50.079
No point in going back.

13:50.579 --> 13:52.373
We'll blend in with the
crowd in the world below.

13:54.625 --> 13:55.584
This way.

14:01.549 --> 14:03.926
Whoa!

14:05.719 --> 14:07.388
Thanks for waiting, Hana-chan.

14:08.305 --> 14:10.057
What's going on, Senpai?

14:10.140 --> 14:13.727
I knew you were bringing a human,
but you didn't mention Daemons!

14:15.938 --> 14:16.981
She can see us.

14:17.064 --> 14:18.566
Sorry.

14:19.567 --> 14:21.569
I'll fill you in while we run.

14:22.236 --> 14:24.780
Get us out of here.

14:24.864 --> 14:26.782
Yuru's in danger.

14:26.866 --> 14:29.201
This is one of the twins?

14:29.285 --> 14:31.287
And these are the Left and Right.

14:32.788 --> 14:33.789
What is this thing?

14:33.873 --> 14:35.875
It's a hunk of metal.

14:35.958 --> 14:38.210
They're not listening.

14:38.294 --> 14:39.879
Nice to meet you, Yuru-kun.

14:39.962 --> 14:41.005
Likewise.

14:41.589 --> 14:46.218
I'm Hana. Dera-senpai and I
work together as daemon retainers.

14:46.844 --> 14:51.015
Left and Right, are there
any daemon wielders nearby?

14:51.098 --> 14:52.725
Nope. None.

14:52.808 --> 14:56.312
Nice. Then let's head somewhere crowded.

14:56.395 --> 14:57.563
Get in, Yuru.

14:57.646 --> 14:58.731
What is this thing?

14:59.315 --> 15:02.234
You want me to get inside
this bizarre contraption?

15:02.735 --> 15:03.819
Right.

15:03.903 --> 15:06.906
It's called an automobile.

15:06.989 --> 15:08.699
It's a vehicle of the world below.

15:09.241 --> 15:13.954
Uh, it's made of metal and stuff,
and this lady is the driver, and...

15:17.833 --> 15:20.669
There are horses in here,
and it goes real fast!

15:22.379 --> 15:23.380
I see.

15:23.464 --> 15:24.840
So that's how it works.

15:24.924 --> 15:25.883
Got it.

15:26.926 --> 15:28.344
Seriously?

15:29.887 --> 15:32.431
Our ride's late.

15:33.098 --> 15:36.477
We're not still inside
the barrier, are we?

15:36.560 --> 15:38.938
We must be outside since
we can get a signal.

15:39.021 --> 15:39.688
WE'RE AT THE SIGN 2 KM FROM THE
OLD HIGASHI VILLAGE TRAILHEAD

15:39.772 --> 15:43.442
Even if we were still inside,
we could just force it open again.

15:44.902 --> 15:46.195
There they are.

15:46.904 --> 15:48.405
Thank you for waiting.

15:48.489 --> 15:50.199
Sounds like you ran into some trouble.

15:50.783 --> 15:52.826
Thanks for coming, Jin-chan.

15:53.494 --> 15:56.413
Thank you for coming all the
way up the mountain, Jin-san.

15:56.497 --> 15:59.124
I heard new Daemons showed up.

15:59.208 --> 16:01.627
Perhaps I should've come with you.

16:02.544 --> 16:04.254
Load her onto the stretcher.

16:04.338 --> 16:06.632
Gabby-chan-san, how are your wounds?

16:06.715 --> 16:08.133
They've stopped bleeding.

16:08.717 --> 16:10.427
I've got an arrowhead in my shoulder.

16:10.511 --> 16:12.096
Could you take it out later?

16:12.179 --> 16:14.223
The shot to my leg went straight through.

16:14.306 --> 16:15.975
Those are serious injuries.

16:16.058 --> 16:18.185
Don't talk about them like
they're little bug bites.

16:18.769 --> 16:20.521
I'm fine.

16:20.604 --> 16:22.439
I'm used to pain.

16:23.774 --> 16:26.568
So, since your brother isn't with you...

16:27.152 --> 16:28.237
He got away.

16:28.737 --> 16:31.031
But you confirmed his existence, yes?

16:31.115 --> 16:32.574
He's alive and well.

16:33.158 --> 16:35.703
He went down the mountain.
You didn't run into him?

16:35.786 --> 16:39.581
No, even though we secured
all the trailheads.

16:40.165 --> 16:42.292
So they escaped another way.

16:42.376 --> 16:44.086
Maybe they're still on the mountain.

16:44.169 --> 16:45.963
If we had choppers...

16:47.297 --> 16:49.842
We lost two choppers and all our soldiers.

16:50.426 --> 16:52.177
The old man won't be happy.

16:52.261 --> 16:54.096
Hang in there, Jin-chan.

16:54.179 --> 16:57.099
Asa's brother fled with a
middle-aged guy called Dera.

16:58.017 --> 16:58.892
Dera.

16:58.976 --> 17:01.645
He's probably the one who
killed the soldiers, too.

17:01.729 --> 17:04.148
Kagemori-san, could Dera be...?

17:05.274 --> 17:07.151
The Tadera.

17:07.735 --> 17:11.488
Why'd we have to choose a day
when a Tadera daemon retainer was around?

17:12.573 --> 17:16.326
I should've brought mine after all.

17:17.953 --> 17:21.582
Anyway, we released the Left and Right,

17:21.665 --> 17:25.961
took down some choppers, and knocked out
the enemy Daemons on our way here.

17:26.045 --> 17:30.132
I took out most of the soldiers I found,
but there were a bunch of them.

17:30.215 --> 17:32.384
They even brought soldiers?

17:32.468 --> 17:34.428
They sound like a pain in the ass.

17:34.511 --> 17:37.973
Right? It's probably the Kagemoris.

17:38.057 --> 17:38.932
The Kagemoris?!

17:39.016 --> 17:41.894
They know my face and name now.

17:42.895 --> 17:45.939
Guess I'll shave. I'll have to move, too.

17:47.524 --> 17:49.860
I wanted to live my life in peace.

17:53.572 --> 17:56.116
I sense Daemons approaching.

17:56.200 --> 17:57.034
Seriously?!

17:57.117 --> 17:59.661
Are we being followed?

17:59.745 --> 18:02.331
Already?

18:02.414 --> 18:03.665
Fret not.

18:05.459 --> 18:08.212
They mean us no harm.

18:09.129 --> 18:10.756
They're old friends.

18:18.138 --> 18:20.390
It's good to see you
again, Left and Right.

18:21.058 --> 18:24.686
If you're here, does that mean
you've found a new master?

18:24.770 --> 18:27.606
Yeah. We haven't been down
the mountain in so long,

18:27.689 --> 18:29.483
we have no idea what's goin' on.

18:29.566 --> 18:31.276
It's been about four hundred years.

18:31.860 --> 18:34.321
This child is our new master.

18:34.404 --> 18:37.324
Oh, how nice. I love children.

18:37.991 --> 18:41.161
He's one of the twins
dividin' night and day.

18:43.956 --> 18:45.707
Well, that won't be easy.

18:47.417 --> 18:49.169
What will you do now?

18:49.253 --> 18:50.420
Who knows?

18:50.504 --> 18:53.841
For now, it seems we'll
be hidin' in a lively village.

18:54.341 --> 18:55.467
I see.

18:56.218 --> 18:58.887
Tell me about it when you return.

19:00.556 --> 19:02.349
Safe travels.

19:05.435 --> 19:06.979
That's the first time I've seen them!

19:07.062 --> 19:09.148
The first time I've seen them!
The first time I've seen them!

19:09.231 --> 19:10.941
They really do exist!

19:11.024 --> 19:12.860
What were those things?

19:12.943 --> 19:14.319
Don't call them things!

19:14.903 --> 19:16.446
That was Oshirasama!

19:16.530 --> 19:20.242
They're a legit god on a whole other
level from your average daemon!

19:20.325 --> 19:22.161
- Legit...?
- The real deal!

19:22.870 --> 19:25.706
I never thought I'd meet them
while I was still alive.

19:25.789 --> 19:28.667
I'm so glad to be alive.

19:29.459 --> 19:33.255
You know, in our village,
we're treated like gods.

19:33.338 --> 19:36.091
Why the disparity in treatment?

19:36.675 --> 19:38.719
So there are all kinds of Daemons.

19:38.802 --> 19:39.845
There sure are.

19:39.928 --> 19:43.515
Us humans just
like sorting them into genres.

19:43.599 --> 19:44.641
Genres...?

19:44.725 --> 19:50.981
As in types or categories,
like gods or spirits.

19:51.064 --> 19:55.277
Some live relaxed lives alongside
humans, like Oshirasama,

19:55.360 --> 20:01.408
others bring luck to their masters
and some encourage criminal activity.

20:01.491 --> 20:05.037
Those dentures that attacked us
were probably a combat type.

20:05.537 --> 20:07.915
The upper and lower jaw form a pair.

20:08.498 --> 20:11.919
I've heard of Daemons gobbling up
their masters if they don't like them.

20:12.836 --> 20:16.840
I'm sorry. It was my call
to let my brother go.

20:16.924 --> 20:19.301
I'll go with you to be reprimanded.

20:19.384 --> 20:21.470
It's not your fault, Asa.

20:21.553 --> 20:23.764
You were protecting me.

20:23.847 --> 20:26.058
Don't worry about it, you two.

20:26.600 --> 20:31.647
The old man will be happy to know
he's alive and off the mountain.

20:31.730 --> 20:36.026
No, seriously. They might've caught me
if Asa hadn't been there.

20:36.693 --> 20:39.071
Were his Daemons that strong?

20:39.154 --> 20:44.451
Yeah, but it was Asa's brother
who shot me with a bow.

20:44.534 --> 20:48.038
First he shut down my mobility,
then my dominant hand.

20:48.121 --> 20:50.290
Your brother is brutal.

20:50.374 --> 20:53.669
He's got the mind of a hunter.

21:03.512 --> 21:04.346
Damn.

21:05.097 --> 21:06.974
It's coming down.

21:07.057 --> 21:11.186
We'll get left behind if we don't
meet up with Kagemori-san soon.

21:11.270 --> 21:12.271
We'd better hur—

21:13.814 --> 21:15.148
It's not here...

21:19.319 --> 21:21.613
We've been here five times already.

21:22.197 --> 21:24.616
We're screwed. We can't leave.

23:27.656 --> 23:28.949
PREVIEW

23:29.032 --> 23:32.160
Flush when you're done.

23:32.244 --> 23:33.203
Guntama Prefecture.

23:33.286 --> 23:34.454
Guntama Prefecture.

23:34.538 --> 23:37.958
Why do I have to marry you?!
